{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist","id":935206,"title":"advise on how to deal with geist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-21T12:39:40-07:00","id":935206,"title":"advise on how to deal with geist","content":"Can anyone offer any insight on how a mortal might get the advantage or even defeat a geist?<br /> <br /> i know a basic human has little to no chance against anything supernatural but sometimes they come with weaknesses like silver for werewolves or fire fore vampires, does anyone have any tips for going up against a geist as a human, or even as a vampire or werewolf? <br /> <br /> Wasn't sure which sub-forum to post this under but i figure hunters would have the most knowledge for dealing with supernatural threats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:37:40-07:00","id":935235,"title":"","content":"Depends on your level of play. Several endowments allow hunters to actually physically damage the deist as well as the sin eater, but at lower tiers the only real way to deal with them is to hide and research until you find a chink in the armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T09:44:56-07:00","id":936590,"title":"","content":"If you run on 2E rules ( like from <b>Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook</b> ) Ephemeral Entity Mortal Interaction can be your tools - just make Geist being high Rank Ghost ( as it was asses to be ) and let PCs to uncover Bane, Ban and makes all those Banishments or Summoning rituals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:43:43-07:00","id":937301,"title":"","content":"i only play 1e at the moment, but basically it seem like they have no obvious weakness.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the responses so far","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:19:14-07:00","id":937406,"title":"","content":"Kill it once, wrap it in some nice, heavy chains, and then dump his ass in concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T06:46:30-07:00","id":937576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=937406#post937406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill it once, wrap it in some nice, heavy chains, and then dump his ass in concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist, not the Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> Geists probably <i>should</i> have bans you can exploit, though. 1E has a generic Ban(e) of Holy Objects for Ghosts, I believe. That might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T22:11:14-07:00","id":937931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=937576#post937576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geist, not the Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> Geists probably <i>should</i> have bans you can exploit, though. 1E has a generic Ban(e) of Holy Objects for Ghosts, I believe. That might work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my bad.<br /> <br /> But yeah, those should work. Failing that, there might be a thaumaturge or psychic who could assist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:17:57-07:00","id":937972,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, premanently getting rid of the Sin-Eater should also get rid of the Geist, sending it's ass back to the underworld, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:06:45-07:00","id":938052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=937972#post937972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, premanently getting rid of the Sin-Eater should also get rid of the Geist, sending it's ass back to the underworld, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>No Sin-Eater is involved, just an UnBargained Geist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T21:21:33-07:00","id":938580,"title":"","content":"Can you stop the geist by getting rid of the sin eater it is attached to?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T01:53:15-07:00","id":938686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=938580#post938580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you stop the geist by getting rid of the sin eater it is attached to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the Sin Eater dies of old age or in a way that the body won't be able to be repaired by plasm, no. After enough deaths it'll be even worse beacause the body will just become Geist's meat puppet. At least I think so, correct me if I'm wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T02:14:27-07:00","id":938693,"title":"","content":"If I'm not mistaken, a geist may choose top revive a Sin Eater beyond the regular 5 times limit (and that without including all the tricks they have to cheat death before getting to that situation) by creating one of the Wretched- but it is a choice. Many geists won't do it out of their personal reasons- but some would prefer having a not very functional meat suit than no meat suit at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:14:27-07:00","id":939612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=938686#post938686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the Sin Eater dies of old age or in a way that the body won't be able to be repaired by plasm, no. After enough deaths it'll be even worse beacause the body will just become Geist's meat puppet. At least I think so, correct me if I'm wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can plasm repair the sin eater if a character manages to blow off its head?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T01:01:21-07:00","id":939995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=939612#post939612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can plasm repair the sin eater if a character manages to blow off its head?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically, a Sin Eater would use plasm to make sure they don't get their head blown off at all - they can spend a plasm to reduce all damage received from a single source to a single bashing damage. They can't outright <i>heal</i> damage unless using a ceremony though, and those not only usually require a <i>lot</i> of plasm to work right, they can't undo such severe damage as a destroyed head. Limbs maybe, but not something as essential as a head.<br /> <br /> As for getting rid of roaming Geists, the most usual way is just to do it the same way one would a normal ghost. Geists may be a lot more powerful than normal ghosts, but they're subject to the same weaknesses save for having anchors. I believe that Project: VALKYRIE has Etheric Rounds that allow a normal gun to do lethal damage to ghosts, which also work against both Geists and Sin Eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:00:46-07:00","id":940775,"title":"","content":"So unlikely as it may be it is possible for hunter, or even a normal mortal to defeat a sin eater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T20:08:35-07:00","id":941009,"title":"","content":"Of course, though it gets more difficult the higher up in rank you go, and the less prepared for killing the killer is. Obviously the more people you have on your side and the less they have on theirs the better as well.<br /> <br /> Spending plasm to reduce damage means less plasm to use powering abilities. It means they can't use plasm-powered manifestations if their Psyche is low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T22:45:13-07:00","id":941705,"title":"","content":"Part of me is asking because our group has recently picked up the Antagonist and Geist the Sin Eater books and i think our story teller might pit us up against some eventually as antagonist even though most of the time our group creates normal mortal characters. We have the 1e core books of VtR, WtF, MtA, and Hunter the vigil but it seems 9 out of 10 times the entire group will go with normal NON-hunter mortals.<br /> <br /> i have very little experience with table top gaming and basically no knowledge of Geist the Sin Eater so i figured i'd ask","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T02:19:14-07:00","id":941777,"title":"","content":"If you want a more balanced Hunter experience, I highly recommend grabbing Mortal Remains, which grants you hunter versions of Chengelings, Prometheans, Sin Eaters, Mummies and Demons. They use Willpower instead of their various fuels, usually, and they also give an interesting view on how to modify dread powers, as well as some new Hunter conspiracies, usually tailored to a specific type of monsters. It does shift towards making things 2e though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:42:15-07:00","id":941934,"title":"","content":"Maybe you should just wait and see what the storyteller's going to do rather than trying to guess and use the forum to metagame.<br /> <br /> Presumably they're not the type to introduce a new antagonist and kill your entire party because it amuses them, and if they introduce an antagonist it would be one your characters could figure out how to defeat in-character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:01:50-07:00","id":942085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=941934#post941934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you should just wait and see what the storyteller's going to do rather than trying to guess and use the forum to metagame.<br /> <br /> Presumably they're not the type to introduce a new antagonist and kill your entire party because it amuses them, and if they introduce an antagonist it would be one your characters could figure out how to defeat in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good point, my apologies. Trying to figure something out is where a lot of the fun comes from and failing to overcome something is bound to happen<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:44:31-07:00","id":942124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/935206-advise-on-how-to-deal-with-geist?p=942085#post942085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point, my apologies. Trying to figure something out is where a lot of the fun comes from and failing to overcome something is bound to happen</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, and there's no reason to apologize. While I know pre-emptive problem solving can be fun, so can encountering something new you've never heard of. Perhaps you should take a look at the Geist book. It's a player book, the only one of its line, and might prepare you at least a little bit while also letting you see how another game is played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:37:48-07:00","id":942209,"title":"","content":"My group decided that TF:V's &quot;Etheric&quot; Endowments could interact with Sin-Eaters in unusual ways. Two main examples:<br /> <br /> Etheric Goggles: Showed a haze around the Sin-Eater, not a discernible image of the Geist per-se, but looking at a Sin-Eater would almost look like some kind of double-exposure camera trick.<br /> <br /> Etheric Rounds: Still do the limited harm to the Sin-Eater as per the normal rule of shooting living beings with them, but it disrupts their Plasm, preventing them from spening it to mitigate the damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:25:27-07:00","id":942271,"title":"","content":"i've gone through the geist book and couldn't find anything that stuck out like silver for werewolves or fire for vampires but at this point i think if my character had a gun available and had to go up against a Sin Eater i'd go for a simple called shot to the head at -3 and hope that three or more successes means the end for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:45:31-07:00","id":942381,"title":"","content":"Sin Eaters generally don't have weaknesses like those, aside from running out of plasm so they can't use their abilities or if they're too powerful - they can get Banes on them from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}